# RULE BUDGET — READ BEFORE ADDING ANYTHING
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Cloudflare stops honouring rules past roughly the 110th-115th non-comment rule
# in this file. Rules below that point are parsed but never fire, silently.
#
#   CURRENT COUNT: 80 rules.  BUDGET: keep it under 100.
#   Check with:  grep -vE '^\s*#|^\s*$' _redirects | wc -l
#
# Measured on production 2026-07-30 by curling crowagent.ai directly:
#   - rule 110 (/get-crowagent-core) FIRED           -> 301
#   - rule 112 (/sign-in)            FIRED           -> 302
#   - rule 114 (/doc/*)              FIRED           -> 200
#   - rule 117 (/tools/*/methodology) DEAD           -> 404
#   - rule 120 (/blog/ppn-002-guide)  DEAD           -> 404
#   - rule 124 (/blog/social-value-themes-explained) DEAD -> 404
# So the previous header's "roughly the 109th" was pessimistic by ~5, but the
# effect is real and the file WAS 126 rules long, i.e. the last 17 were dead —
# including a link the site's own /resources page pointed at.
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# HOW CLOUDFLARE PAGES ACTUALLY BEHAVES (all measured live 2026-07-30, not
# inferred — re-measure before contradicting any of it)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# 1. FIRST MATCH WINS, top-down. A rule below a rule that matches never runs.
#
# 2. CF's own URL canonicalisation runs BEFORE this file is consulted:
#      /about.html   -> 308 -> /about      (flat file exists)
#      /about/       -> 308 -> /about      (flat file exists, slash stripped)
#      /sectors      -> 308 -> /sectors/   (directory exists, slash ADDED)
#    Consequence: a URL form that CF canonicalises away can never be the form a
#    crawler indexed, because it never returned 200. That is why this file no
#    longer carries `.html` twins or flat-path trailing-slash twins for deleted
#    pages: those forms were always a redirect, never a page. See the deletion
#    note in each block.
#
# 3. Canonicalisation only happens when something exists at the target. With no
#    file present, /foo.html and /foo/ both 404 outright — they are NOT rewritten
#    to /foo. So for a DELETED page, only the extensionless no-slash form is worth
#    a rule, and directory-backed pages keep their trailing-slash form because
#    that WAS their 200 URL.
#
# 4. An existing static asset is served BEFORE this file is consulted, so no rule
#    can shadow a file that is actually deployed. Verified: /styles.css still
#    returns 200 (its 301-to-minified rule has never worked and has been deleted),
#    and the 254 tracked files under tests/, .dev-tools/, specs/ and scripts/ are
#    publicly readable no matter what is written here. The only real fix is to give
#    the Pages project a build output directory instead of publishing the repo
#    root. That is an infrastructure change, flagged to the owner, not fakeable
#    here.
#
# 5. A 3xx rule DOES override a file that exists (unlike a 404 rule). This is why
#    the methodology guard rules further down matter: without them the
#    `/tools/*/methodology` splat would 301 the live PPN 002 methodology page away.
#
# 6. CF Pages serves a top-level /404.html with a 404 status for any unmatched
#    request all on its own. Verified: the branded 404 body is returned today even
#    though the `/*` splat is rule 126 and therefore dead. The splat is kept as
#    belt-and-braces, and now sits inside the honoured range.
#
# BEFORE APPENDING ANY RULE: add it ABOVE the `/*` splat at the bottom, never
# after. To verify, run:
#   awk '/^\/\*[[:space:]]+\/404\.html/{f=1;next} f && /^\//{print NR": "$0}' _redirects
# That must print nothing.

# ── 1. CASE-FOLDING FOR THE PascalCase ASSET DIRECTORIES ─────────────────────
# CODE-AUDIT-023. The repo carries `Assets/` and `Doc/` in PascalCase. CF Pages is
# case-sensitive (verified: /ASSETS/css/sovereign-cmdk.css 404s while
# /Assets/css/sovereign-cmdk.css 200s), but some external links and crawlers
# normalise to lowercase. These sit at the very top because they are the only
# rules whose failure breaks rendering rather than just a link.
# DELETED 2026-07-30: `/assets/branding-logo/* -> /Assets/Branding%20Logo/:splat`.
# Two independent reasons it was useless. (a) `Assets/Branding Logo/` does not
# exist in this repo any more — the destination was a dead path. (b) Even if it
# had existed, `/assets/*` above it matches every /assets/ request first, so the
# rule could never have fired from where it sat.
/assets/*               /Assets/:splat               200
/doc/*                  /Doc/:splat                  200

# ── 2. www → apex (DEF-008) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Layer 1: CF DNS CNAME www → crowagent.ai. Layer 2: CF Redirect Rules. Layer 3
# (this line, defence in depth). Single direction only; there is no apex→www
# counterpart anywhere, so a loop is not possible.
https://www.crowagent.ai/*  https://crowagent.ai/:splat  301!

